1
00:00:04,767 --> 00:00:11,733
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,767 --> 00:00:32,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:35,067
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,767 --> 00:00:40,900
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,267 --> 00:00:43,867
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:45,200
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:46,300
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,733 --> 00:00:48,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,133
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,433 --> 00:00:53,500
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,367
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,567 --> 00:00:58,100
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,033
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:02,700
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,067 --> 00:01:06,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:09,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:11,467
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,467 --> 00:01:12,800
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:14,367
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,667 --> 00:01:22,667
<i>Her car was riddled
with bullets.</i>

21
00:01:22,667 --> 00:01:24,467
<i>Is there already
a prime suspect?</i>

22
00:01:24,467 --> 00:01:26,000
<i> None other than the Zafras.</i>

23
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,700
<i> We have company this late?</i>

24
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:28,700
<i> This is Pia.</i>

25
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:31,900
<i>So we have a mole
in the NCIA now.</i>

26
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:32,967
<i> I'm not your mole.</i>

27
00:01:32,967 --> 00:01:35,300
<i> I am your asset.</i>

28
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:36,467
<i> Someone ambushed Sam.</i>

29
00:01:36,467 --> 00:01:37,833
<i>Where did you last see
Sam's car?</i>

30
00:01:37,833 --> 00:01:39,033
<i> At Soriano Street.</i>

31
00:01:39,633 --> 00:01:40,933
We opened fire in her direction.

32
00:01:40,967 --> 00:01:42,500
<i>We got her
and she fell into the river.</i>

33
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:44,733
<i> If there is no body,
death is not a certainty.</i>

34
00:01:44,733 --> 00:01:48,467
<i>So don't come back here
until you confirm she's dead!</i>

35
00:01:48,467 --> 00:01:50,300
<i>I pray she comes
into my life soon, Lord.</i>

36
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:51,967
<i> You can drop her to me
if You want to.</i>

37
00:01:51,967 --> 00:01:53,100
<i> Oh!</i>

38
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:54,933
<i> - Who is that?!
</i>- And why does she have a gun?!

39
00:01:54,933 --> 00:01:55,967
<i> She's injured.</i>

40
00:01:55,967 --> 00:01:57,533
<i> Get some medicine.</i>

41
00:01:57,533 --> 00:01:58,767
<i> Could someone be chasing her?</i>

42
00:01:58,767 --> 00:02:00,267
<i> That's why she came
from the roof.</i>

43
00:02:02,767 --> 00:02:05,867
[LUCAS] We won't stop
until we find that woman.

44
00:02:06,267 --> 00:02:09,367
Boss, where are we
going to find her?

45
00:02:09,367 --> 00:02:12,700
We've searched every nook
and cranny in the area.

46
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:14,000
Boss,

47
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,667
even if we dive into the river,

48
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:18,467
we won't find anything
but dirt and garbage.

49
00:02:18,467 --> 00:02:19,733
Just do as I say.

50
00:02:19,733 --> 00:02:21,400
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

51
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,867
Even if she was swept away,

52
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:25,400
she's unlikely to be far.

53
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:27,133
Where does this river lead?

54
00:02:27,133 --> 00:02:28,800
It's quite long, boss.

55
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,367
Then start searching.

56
00:02:31,367 --> 00:02:32,767
But stay alert.

57
00:02:32,767 --> 00:02:36,333
She might be lying low, waiting
for the right time to escape.

58
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,167
[LEE] Copy, boss.

59
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,233
All of you, move now!

60
00:02:41,233 --> 00:02:43,800
- Come on!
- Let's go!

61
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:49,367
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

62
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,400
Come on!

63
00:02:52,567 --> 00:02:53,867
[MUSIC FADES]

64
00:02:53,867 --> 00:02:56,400
Is that why you promoted her
to manager?

65
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:58,900
- So you could win her over?
- [CHUCKLES]

66
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:00,033
Well...

67
00:03:00,967 --> 00:03:03,033
- Pa.
- Yes?

68
00:03:03,033 --> 00:03:05,400
[INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER]

69
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,933
Did I hear that right?

70
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:09,033
Does Ibyang know?

71
00:03:09,033 --> 00:03:10,700
- [ALCOHOL SLOSHING]
- [CHUCKLES]

72
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:15,333
Django, I don't need
to ask her permission.

73
00:03:15,333 --> 00:03:18,733
I am the owner of BeerGin.

74
00:03:18,733 --> 00:03:20,167
What if Rudy finds out
about this?

75
00:03:20,167 --> 00:03:22,167
To hell with Rudy.

76
00:03:22,633 --> 00:03:26,367
I'm targeting the people
close to Gabo.

77
00:03:26,367 --> 00:03:27,533
Got it?

78
00:03:27,533 --> 00:03:28,800
[ROMY] Think of it this way.

79
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,900
If she wins Betchay
over completely,

80
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:33,333
it's like you've already
gotten back at Gabo.

81
00:03:33,333 --> 00:03:34,433
Makes sense.

82
00:03:35,133 --> 00:03:37,833
And if you manage
to charm her enough,

83
00:03:37,833 --> 00:03:39,367
she might open up

84
00:03:40,033 --> 00:03:42,300
and tell you what
Gabo's real work is.

85
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:43,533
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:03:43,533 --> 00:03:45,500
Spot on!

87
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,033
- [PAQUITO] Have a drink, Romy.
- [GLASS THUDS]

88
00:03:52,067 --> 00:03:54,067
- [MUSIC FADES]
- [CRICKETS CHIRP IN DISTANCE]

89
00:03:54,367 --> 00:03:56,133
Call your sister this instant!

90
00:03:56,133 --> 00:03:57,400
- Call her!
- [KAREN] Ma'am...

91
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,133
You won't be able to call her

92
00:03:59,133 --> 00:04:01,667
because we found
her cell phone in the car,

93
00:04:01,667 --> 00:04:04,000
and we already took it
as evidence.

94
00:04:04,267 --> 00:04:07,333
The CCTV footage in the area,
have you secured them?

95
00:04:07,333 --> 00:04:10,333
For now, were getting as much
information as we can.

96
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:11,833
- [GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]
- [ISOBEL CRYING]

97
00:04:11,833 --> 00:04:15,000
Max, it'll break me
if something bad happens

98
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,333
to my youngest!

99
00:04:16,333 --> 00:04:19,000
[MAX] Ma, now is not the time
to overthink!

100
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,867
- [SOBS] No!
- [SOFTLY] Okay?

101
00:04:20,867 --> 00:04:24,433
We're going to find
and save Sam.

102
00:04:24,433 --> 00:04:25,733
Sit down.

103
00:04:25,733 --> 00:04:30,200
- [CRYING CONTINUES]
- [GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

104
00:04:30,233 --> 00:04:31,600
Oh my god...

105
00:04:32,033 --> 00:04:36,367
Tonight is the greatest night
of my career in the NCIA!

106
00:04:36,367 --> 00:04:38,600
All because you got rid
of Jacinto!

107
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:41,700
We've avenged you
against the Jacintos.

108
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:42,800
On your behalf.

109
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:44,033
[PIA] Thank you.

110
00:04:44,733 --> 00:04:46,800
[MARIANO] How's your agency?

111
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:49,200
Has Samantha
been confirmed dead?

112
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:50,233
[DEBORAH SCOFFS]

113
00:04:50,233 --> 00:04:52,000
Come on, Mariano.

114
00:04:52,833 --> 00:04:55,167
She's definitely gone.

115
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:59,400
Besides, Pia didn't come here
for that.

116
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,100
She's not here
to talk about Samantha.

117
00:05:03,033 --> 00:05:04,733
What are we going to talk about?

118
00:05:04,733 --> 00:05:07,933
All I care about
is my son, Victor.

119
00:05:07,933 --> 00:05:10,933
Are you doing anything
to get him out of jail?

120
00:05:10,933 --> 00:05:12,500
Tell me more about Delgado.

121
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:15,900
Can we easily buy him off?

122
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:16,967
Don't worry,

123
00:05:17,967 --> 00:05:20,300
I can easily manipulate
that old man.

124
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:21,667
Ma'am, sir.

125
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,100
I'm close to getting
Victor out of prison.

126
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,567
Especially now
that Jacinto is gone.

127
00:05:30,267 --> 00:05:32,767
Victor's freedom or escape?

128
00:05:32,767 --> 00:05:33,833
Dear...

129
00:05:34,733 --> 00:05:36,833
figure it out.

130
00:05:36,833 --> 00:05:38,467
Victor is getting impatient.

131
00:05:40,033 --> 00:05:41,567
We are too.

132
00:05:41,567 --> 00:05:44,300
The people getting in the way
of my plan are gone.

133
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,033
- [PIA SCOFFS]
- [TEACUP CLANKS]

134
00:05:46,033 --> 00:05:47,600
This should be easy.

135
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:49,033
If you think about it,

136
00:05:49,033 --> 00:05:52,633
NCIA is basically
in the palm of my hands.

137
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:56,467
Put your money
where your mouth is.

138
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:06,467
[MUSIC FADES]

139
00:06:08,367 --> 00:06:10,533
- [IBYANG] You done?
- Yes.

140
00:06:10,533 --> 00:06:12,533
- Ibyang.
- [IBYANG] What?

141
00:06:12,533 --> 00:06:14,200
- Have you heard?
- About what?

142
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,100
Betchay is now the manager
of BeerGin.

143
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:18,267
- What?!
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

144
00:06:18,267 --> 00:06:19,900
Since when? Who said so?

145
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:21,067
Papa did.

146
00:06:21,067 --> 00:06:23,500
Seriously? That was quick.
She just got in.

147
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:25,767
And now she's the manager?
Unbelievable.

148
00:06:25,767 --> 00:06:28,333
That bastard Paquito.

149
00:06:28,333 --> 00:06:29,833
Your father is shameless!

150
00:06:29,833 --> 00:06:31,567
- I'll show him--
- Hold up, hold up!

151
00:06:31,567 --> 00:06:32,667
Relax!

152
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:35,700
Oh, please. It's like
you don't know him at all.

153
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:38,367
Your father
is making a fool out of me!

154
00:06:38,367 --> 00:06:42,200
He knew I was mad when he hired
Betchay to work at BeerGin!

155
00:06:42,233 --> 00:06:43,967
And now he had the nerve
to promote her?!

156
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,567
Oh, come on.
You know how his mind works.

157
00:06:48,567 --> 00:06:50,633
You know he did that
for a reason.

158
00:06:50,633 --> 00:06:53,433
And we'll benefit from it,
so just trust him for now.

159
00:06:53,433 --> 00:06:56,167
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

160
00:06:56,167 --> 00:06:57,333
[MUSIC FADES]

161
00:06:57,333 --> 00:06:59,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

162
00:06:59,333 --> 00:07:00,367
Mom.

163
00:07:00,367 --> 00:07:01,733
[ISOBEL SOBS]

164
00:07:01,733 --> 00:07:04,533
What if we involve
the media in this?

165
00:07:04,533 --> 00:07:06,500
That could help
find Sam more easily.

166
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:08,567
So we can find her immediately!

167
00:07:08,567 --> 00:07:11,500
The media could complicate
the investigation.

168
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:12,333
Auntie.

169
00:07:13,833 --> 00:07:16,267
If Sam was kidnapped
by bad people,

170
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:19,133
and they find out
we're looking for her,

171
00:07:19,133 --> 00:07:20,533
they would be rattled.

172
00:07:20,533 --> 00:07:23,300
And they may do something
to harm Sam.

173
00:07:24,467 --> 00:07:26,167
They have a point, Mom.

174
00:07:26,167 --> 00:07:28,167
Okay? We got this.

175
00:07:29,333 --> 00:07:32,867
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

176
00:07:32,867 --> 00:07:33,900
Dad.

177
00:07:36,433 --> 00:07:38,467
I called Domingo.

178
00:07:38,467 --> 00:07:40,600
I asked him to find Sam.

179
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,467
Dad, I'll help them.

180
00:07:42,467 --> 00:07:43,800
No, no, no.

181
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:46,167
Don't do that. Leave it to them.
Don't go.

182
00:07:46,167 --> 00:07:49,167
Mom, let me do this
for my sister.

183
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:53,500
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:54,567
[MUSIC FADES]

185
00:07:56,367 --> 00:08:03,300
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:08:18,300 --> 00:08:25,267
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

187
00:08:36,733 --> 00:08:37,700
Auntie.

188
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:40,200
I already changed her clothes.

189
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,833
Her wound isn't deep.

190
00:08:41,833 --> 00:08:44,633
She was just grazed
by a bullet.

191
00:08:44,833 --> 00:08:47,433
Mameng, do you think
she's safe here?

192
00:08:48,667 --> 00:08:52,033
Maybe it'll be better
if we take her to the hospital.

193
00:08:52,033 --> 00:08:53,933
I think so too.

194
00:08:53,933 --> 00:08:56,667
She needs to be checked.
She might have an infection.

195
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:59,567
- You're right.
- Pa, it's dangerous.

196
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:02,733
If we get her out of the house,

197
00:09:02,733 --> 00:09:05,167
the people who are chasing her
might see her.

198
00:09:05,167 --> 00:09:06,767
You know, Gabo,

199
00:09:06,767 --> 00:09:08,167
I thought of that too.

200
00:09:08,167 --> 00:09:11,900
We might get dragged into this
and put our lives in danger.

201
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:15,367
Auntie,

202
00:09:15,367 --> 00:09:16,967
she's in bad shape.

203
00:09:17,933 --> 00:09:19,600
Her life is in danger.

204
00:09:20,267 --> 00:09:21,800
We need to protect her.

205
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:28,733
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

206
00:09:33,433 --> 00:09:35,667
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

207
00:09:35,667 --> 00:09:37,900
What I initially did
for you was easy.

208
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:40,233
I was just passing
on information.

209
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:42,233
But this?

210
00:09:42,967 --> 00:09:44,267
This is dangerous.

211
00:09:44,267 --> 00:09:46,267
You are the Head of Research!

212
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,333
More than anyone else...

213
00:09:50,167 --> 00:09:53,967
You have the ability
to manipulate the case.

214
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:55,867
What's in it for me?

215
00:09:56,700 --> 00:09:58,400
Whatever you want.

216
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:02,167
A mansion, a sports car,
a business!

217
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,200
[DEBORAH] You want
your own resort?

218
00:10:05,933 --> 00:10:07,200
Your own building?

219
00:10:07,833 --> 00:10:08,900
Anything.

220
00:10:10,033 --> 00:10:11,500
[PIA INHALES]

221
00:10:13,733 --> 00:10:14,800
A resort?

222
00:10:15,633 --> 00:10:17,100
That's 50 million pesos.

223
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,167
A mansion?

224
00:10:20,033 --> 00:10:22,000
20 to 30 million pesos.

225
00:10:22,833 --> 00:10:25,600
A car? 15 million.

226
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:28,200
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

227
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:31,467
Your offers don't even amount
to 100 million pesos.

228
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:35,367
That's such a small amount
considering my big reputation

229
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:38,433
and my career that I've been
taking care of for years.

230
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:40,367
[MARIANO SIGHS]

231
00:10:40,367 --> 00:10:43,567
What more do you want?
We'll give it!

232
00:10:43,567 --> 00:10:45,267
Jewelry. Gold!

233
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:51,367
We're talking about your son's
life imprisonment here.

234
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:54,933
What if we mess up?

235
00:10:55,667 --> 00:10:57,967
They'll be able to trace
those properties.

236
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:02,300
[DEBORAH] How about
we give you the cash?

237
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:04,533
Use it however you like.

238
00:11:05,267 --> 00:11:06,367
How much?

239
00:11:06,367 --> 00:11:11,167
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

240
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,800
How much do you want?

241
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:17,067
150 million pesos.

242
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:20,667
I'll do everything
you tell me to.

243
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,267
However...

244
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,867
I wouldn't know when.

245
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:29,833
It's a long process.

246
00:11:29,833 --> 00:11:35,533
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

247
00:11:35,533 --> 00:11:37,100
What about you in the NCIA?

248
00:11:37,967 --> 00:11:41,833
Don't you even have a clue
on who could've done this?

249
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:43,833
We think it's the Zafras.

250
00:11:46,267 --> 00:11:47,933
How about the recent case?

251
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:50,167
[SEBASTIAN] That's unlikely.

252
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:52,867
This morning, one of
our agents was killed.

253
00:11:52,867 --> 00:11:55,867
He's supposed to be a witness
to the Victor Zafra case.

254
00:11:55,867 --> 00:11:57,867
And all evidence leads
to the Zafras.

255
00:11:58,667 --> 00:11:59,933
You see?!

256
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:03,000
Someone died this morning,

257
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,067
and they plan to do
the same thing

258
00:12:05,067 --> 00:12:06,567
- to Sam!
- [MAX] Ma.

259
00:12:06,567 --> 00:12:09,433
That's why I told her
to drop this case!

260
00:12:10,167 --> 00:12:12,033
Because she'll go up against
the Zafras!

261
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:16,633
Uh, sir. Ma'am.

262
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:18,433
We promise you.

263
00:12:18,433 --> 00:12:20,067
We will do everything
to find Sam.

264
00:12:21,633 --> 00:12:23,200
We have to get going now.

265
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:24,833
We have to return
to the crime scene.

266
00:12:24,833 --> 00:12:26,300
- Thank you.
- I'll walk you out.

267
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:27,600
Thank you.

268
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:34,733
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

269
00:12:37,233 --> 00:12:39,133
[LUGGAGE THUDS]

270
00:12:43,633 --> 00:12:44,633
[LUGGAGE THUDS]

271
00:12:45,533 --> 00:12:47,333
75 million pesos.

272
00:12:48,967 --> 00:12:52,433
Once Victor goes free,
we'll give you the other half.

273
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:56,633
You're cautious, huh?

274
00:12:58,367 --> 00:13:02,867
In the world I live in,
I have to be cautious.

275
00:13:02,867 --> 00:13:05,067
I have to be cunning.

276
00:13:05,067 --> 00:13:08,433
If not,
everyone will eat you alive.

277
00:13:10,167 --> 00:13:11,667
Well, I'm also cautious.

278
00:13:14,967 --> 00:13:17,867
Prepare the remaining
75 million pesos

279
00:13:17,867 --> 00:13:19,333
before Victor is released.

280
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:22,267
We'll do an
on-the-spot transaction.

281
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:29,033
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

282
00:13:29,033 --> 00:13:29,967
Mom.

283
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:32,833
- [ISOBEL EXHALES]
- You should rest.

284
00:13:36,667 --> 00:13:38,033
I'll take care of it.

285
00:13:38,033 --> 00:13:39,900
[ISOBEL BREATHES DEEPLY]

286
00:13:41,867 --> 00:13:42,800
Max.

287
00:13:44,667 --> 00:13:46,400
You find her,
and you bring her home.

288
00:13:51,633 --> 00:13:54,067
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

289
00:13:54,067 --> 00:14:01,000
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

290
00:14:02,567 --> 00:14:05,500
[LUGGAGE RATTLING]

291
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:07,433
- Arturo, drop her off.
- No.

292
00:14:08,467 --> 00:14:09,533
I can manage.

293
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:13,433
[SLAP LANDS]

294
00:14:14,067 --> 00:14:15,067
This is mine.

295
00:14:17,567 --> 00:14:19,367
[LUGGAGE ROLLING]

296
00:14:19,367 --> 00:14:20,433
I'll handle it.

297
00:14:26,267 --> 00:14:33,167
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

298
00:14:34,267 --> 00:14:36,533
Are you sure we can trust her?

299
00:14:37,767 --> 00:14:40,500
We're talking about
150 million pesos here.

300
00:14:41,133 --> 00:14:43,333
That's just chump change!

301
00:14:43,333 --> 00:14:46,500
That's nothing compared
to Victor's freedom.

302
00:14:48,233 --> 00:14:49,500
But...

303
00:14:51,167 --> 00:14:53,733
She can't even say
when she'll release him!

304
00:14:54,433 --> 00:14:58,600
Well, at least we got
things moving.

305
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:07,800
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

306
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:08,767
[GLASS THUDS]

307
00:15:18,867 --> 00:15:19,900
[RICARDO EXHALES]

308
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:20,967
[BOTTLE CLINKS]

309
00:15:20,967 --> 00:15:23,067
- [ALCOHOL POURING]
- [BOTTLE THUDS]

310
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:24,867
[GLASS THUDS]

311
00:15:28,267 --> 00:15:30,900
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

312
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:31,933
Manny.

313
00:15:33,133 --> 00:15:35,867
I need intel
on where to find the Zafras.

314
00:15:36,567 --> 00:15:39,067
Boss, what are you planning?

315
00:15:39,767 --> 00:15:41,100
What are we going to do?

316
00:15:41,767 --> 00:15:42,900
They will pay.

317
00:15:43,733 --> 00:15:50,633
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

318
00:15:52,767 --> 00:15:59,733
[MUSIC TURNS UNEASY]

319
00:16:09,467 --> 00:16:10,633
Poor thing.

320
00:16:11,267 --> 00:16:13,167
Good thing she wasn't hit badly.

321
00:16:15,667 --> 00:16:19,133
And she's lucky
she fell through our roof.

322
00:16:20,700 --> 00:16:23,333
I wonder who her parents are.

323
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:27,367
We should tell her family
where she is.

324
00:16:27,367 --> 00:16:29,567
They must be worried about her.

325
00:16:29,567 --> 00:16:31,067
- Yeah.
- [MAMENG] Or why don't

326
00:16:31,067 --> 00:16:33,133
we report it to the NLEA?

327
00:16:33,133 --> 00:16:35,167
Auntie, don't! It's dangerous.

328
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:39,700
We still don't know
who she was fighting against.

329
00:16:42,233 --> 00:16:45,700
Maybe it's better for her
to recover here first.

330
00:16:47,933 --> 00:16:49,100
When she's better...

331
00:16:50,533 --> 00:16:52,200
then we'll look for her parents.

332
00:16:52,767 --> 00:16:57,300
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

333
00:17:03,467 --> 00:17:05,233
[MAN] Boss, they're here.

334
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:09,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

335
00:17:11,233 --> 00:17:12,467
Your father?

336
00:17:12,967 --> 00:17:14,400
He's on his way.

337
00:17:15,033 --> 00:17:16,967
Let's wait for him.

338
00:17:17,867 --> 00:17:19,300
He sent me ahead.

339
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:21,300
You can tell me what you need.

340
00:17:21,300 --> 00:17:23,400
We came all the way here
to First Creek.

341
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:25,500
I'm only here to talk
to Paquito.

342
00:17:26,967 --> 00:17:28,733
You don't trust me?

343
00:17:28,733 --> 00:17:30,200
You think I'm some nobody?

344
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,700
[CHUCKLING]

345
00:17:31,700 --> 00:17:33,033
There it is...

346
00:17:33,033 --> 00:17:35,267
That arrogance of yours

347
00:17:35,267 --> 00:17:38,300
is why people are still
looking for your father.

348
00:17:38,300 --> 00:17:39,467
You asshole!

349
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:41,600
- [OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]
- They've got guns!

350
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:43,133
- Move!
- Cops!

351
00:17:43,133 --> 00:17:47,833
[TENSE MUSIC SWELLS]

352
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:55,600
Wait!

353
00:17:56,900 --> 00:18:03,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

354
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:07,300
Just ignore them.

355
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:09,000
- Let's go.
- Whoa!

356
00:18:12,767 --> 00:18:14,000
Who are you guys?

357
00:18:15,633 --> 00:18:17,233
Looking sharp, huh?

358
00:18:17,767 --> 00:18:18,967
Where's the party?

359
00:18:18,967 --> 00:18:21,200
[CHUCKLES]

360
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:24,733
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

361
00:18:25,300 --> 00:18:26,733
You're outsiders.

362
00:18:31,633 --> 00:18:33,800
I'm the king of Tondo.

363
00:18:34,867 --> 00:18:37,867
Everyone has to come
through me before they get in!

364
00:18:38,433 --> 00:18:39,867
What do you want?

365
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:44,500
Bro...

366
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:47,167
a little something for me.

367
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:50,700
If you want to get through.

368
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:54,267
Lao.

369
00:19:00,333 --> 00:19:01,433
Here.

370
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,200
Is this enough?

371
00:19:08,467 --> 00:19:09,567
There.

372
00:19:09,567 --> 00:19:11,167
You're pretty easy to deal with.

373
00:19:11,167 --> 00:19:12,967
- [DJANGO LAUGHING]
- [BLOW LANDS]

374
00:19:12,967 --> 00:19:15,567
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [MEN GRUNTING]

375
00:19:15,567 --> 00:19:16,600
[THUDS]

376
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:19,600
[MEN GRUNTING]

377
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:25,800
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

378
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:28,767
The thing I hate most
is people messing with me!

379
00:19:29,367 --> 00:19:31,033
Go ahead!
Pull the trigger!

380
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:34,233
You're just cocky because
you got the jump on me!

381
00:19:34,233 --> 00:19:36,767
We can take all of you down
right now!

382
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:38,400
Don't you know who we are?

383
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:40,333
We'll show you
who the Zafras are!

384
00:19:40,333 --> 00:19:42,200
[PAQUITO] Hold on! Hold on!

385
00:19:42,900 --> 00:19:44,500
What's all this about?

386
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:46,967
Everyone, calm down.

387
00:19:46,967 --> 00:19:48,867
Let's talk this out.

388
00:19:48,867 --> 00:19:50,300
Calm down, calm down!

389
00:19:50,300 --> 00:19:51,967
I heard you earlier...

390
00:19:52,933 --> 00:19:54,467
You're Zafras?

391
00:19:54,467 --> 00:19:56,400
Are you Mariano's son?

392
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:58,567
Lower your guns.

393
00:19:58,567 --> 00:20:00,433
We're on the same side here.

394
00:20:00,433 --> 00:20:02,567
Hold on, I'll call your father.

395
00:20:07,933 --> 00:20:11,067
[PHONE VIBRATING]

396
00:20:14,067 --> 00:20:15,233
Hello?

397
00:20:15,233 --> 00:20:16,567
Who's this?

398
00:20:16,567 --> 00:20:19,900
It's Paquito
from Ginintuang Lupa.

399
00:20:19,900 --> 00:20:21,433
What do you need?

400
00:20:21,433 --> 00:20:24,433
Arturo, is Mariano there?

401
00:20:24,433 --> 00:20:25,933
Is this important?

402
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:27,200
What is this about?

403
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:30,667
His son is here.

404
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:35,367
And I don't know what he's
doing here in our territory.

405
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:38,533
Sir.

406
00:20:40,933 --> 00:20:41,967
Who's this?

407
00:20:45,733 --> 00:20:46,833
Hello?

408
00:20:46,833 --> 00:20:48,667
Boss Mariano.

409
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,300
It's Paquito.

410
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:54,367
You probably don't remember me.

411
00:20:55,833 --> 00:21:00,933
Well, your son is here.

412
00:21:00,933 --> 00:21:03,967
And I don't know
what he's doing here.

413
00:21:04,467 --> 00:21:05,600
Paquito...

414
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:09,400
don't you dare lay a hand
on my son.

415
00:21:10,633 --> 00:21:15,933
Boss Mariano,
if you need any help,

416
00:21:15,933 --> 00:21:17,367
just give me a call.

417
00:21:17,367 --> 00:21:18,533
I'll take care of it.

418
00:21:18,867 --> 00:21:22,900
If I need you, you'll know.

419
00:21:26,367 --> 00:21:27,433
There.

420
00:21:28,167 --> 00:21:29,867
I called your father.

421
00:21:29,867 --> 00:21:31,233
Lower your guns.

422
00:21:33,267 --> 00:21:35,367
We're not enemies here.

423
00:21:35,367 --> 00:21:37,500
Sorry about my son.

424
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,100
Django, get up.

425
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:46,167
Lower your guns.

426
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,867
What do you need?

427
00:21:48,867 --> 00:21:50,600
We have a transaction here.

428
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:51,833
Okay, kid.

429
00:21:51,833 --> 00:21:53,900
Tell your father

430
00:21:53,900 --> 00:21:55,800
if he wants to do business here,

431
00:21:56,533 --> 00:21:57,867
I'll take care of it.

432
00:21:57,867 --> 00:21:59,167
We don't need you.

433
00:21:59,167 --> 00:22:03,967
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

434
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:06,433
Let us through.

435
00:22:15,467 --> 00:22:17,100
Who was that?

436
00:22:17,100 --> 00:22:18,267
What an asshole.

437
00:22:18,267 --> 00:22:19,833
[PAQUITO] Django.

438
00:22:19,833 --> 00:22:22,900
That's the son of the guy
who used to hire me for hits.

439
00:22:22,900 --> 00:22:26,133
He's a Zafra,
so he's got a big mouth!

440
00:22:26,133 --> 00:22:27,733
Don't mind him.

441
00:22:27,733 --> 00:22:29,833
We can make some money off this.

442
00:22:30,767 --> 00:22:33,467
That's what I like to hear.
Making money.

443
00:22:35,567 --> 00:22:36,933
- Rudy?
- Dante.

444
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:40,533
- I've got some news.
- What?

445
00:22:40,533 --> 00:22:45,533
Some of our neighbors
saw armed men lurking around.

446
00:22:45,533 --> 00:22:47,300
Did you tell them she's here?

447
00:22:47,733 --> 00:22:48,867
No.

448
00:22:48,900 --> 00:22:51,300
I just played dumb and
asked some questions.

449
00:22:52,033 --> 00:22:55,100
But it seems like they're
talking about this woman.

450
00:22:55,100 --> 00:22:56,600
- Oh, no.
- This is bad.

451
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:59,633
No, let's do this instead.

452
00:22:59,633 --> 00:23:01,500
I think we should let her rest
for now.

453
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:04,767
Then we'll make sure
to lock all the doors.

454
00:23:04,767 --> 00:23:07,633
Because the people
looking for her

455
00:23:07,633 --> 00:23:09,100
might track her down here.

456
00:23:09,100 --> 00:23:11,600
They might find out
we hid her in our house.

457
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,733
Right. Let's make sure
the doors are locked

458
00:23:13,733 --> 00:23:15,267
and the windows are shut.
Come on.

459
00:23:15,267 --> 00:23:16,567
- Okay.
- Come on.

460
00:23:20,533 --> 00:23:27,433
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

461
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:44,067
<i>I don't know why you
ended up here with us.</i>

462
00:23:49,067 --> 00:23:50,767
<i> Is fate playing games with us?</i>

463
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:53,633
<i>Why does it keep
bringing us together?</i>

464
00:23:54,567 --> 00:24:01,433
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

465
00:24:06,867 --> 00:24:08,333
<i> But don't worry.</i>

466
00:24:09,033 --> 00:24:10,633
<i> I won't abandon you.</i>

467
00:24:12,633 --> 00:24:15,033
<i>As long as you're
under my protection,</i>

468
00:24:15,033 --> 00:24:18,200
<i>I'll make sure
nothing happens to you.</i>

469
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:19,767
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

470
00:24:23,167 --> 00:24:24,467
[SIGHS SOFTLY]

471
00:24:26,333 --> 00:24:27,900
Who's Paquito?

472
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:30,700
What does he need?

473
00:24:31,367 --> 00:24:34,767
He was one of my men
back at Ginintuang Lupa.

474
00:24:34,767 --> 00:24:37,400
He said Lucas passed by.

475
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:42,400
Ginintuang Lupa
is near Soriano Street.

476
00:24:42,400 --> 00:24:48,200
Why don't you ask Paquito
to help find Samantha's body?

477
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:50,400
I don't trust him to do that.

478
00:24:52,733 --> 00:24:56,800
And no one must find out
about our true intentions.

479
00:24:58,067 --> 00:24:59,867
And most importantly,

480
00:24:59,867 --> 00:25:04,900
no one can find out
we took out Samantha Jacinto.

481
00:25:07,133 --> 00:25:08,267
Well...

482
00:25:09,100 --> 00:25:10,167
You're right.

483
00:25:11,900 --> 00:25:14,733
The more people get involved,

484
00:25:15,967 --> 00:25:18,167
the more complicated
the situation becomes.

485
00:25:20,633 --> 00:25:22,567
The harder it'll be
to get rid of them.

486
00:25:22,567 --> 00:25:29,600
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

487
00:25:39,367 --> 00:25:41,400
Santos, here are
the signed documents.

488
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:42,733
- Thank you, sir.
- Alright.

489
00:25:42,733 --> 00:25:43,767
[UMALI] Yes, sir?

490
00:25:43,767 --> 00:25:46,733
Umali, I received a call
from General Jacinto.

491
00:25:46,733 --> 00:25:48,767
Head over to Soriano Street.

492
00:25:48,767 --> 00:25:52,567
He said his daughter,
Agent Sam Jacinto, was ambushed.

493
00:25:52,567 --> 00:25:54,500
They only recovered
her vehicle.

494
00:25:55,400 --> 00:25:57,500
Alright, sir.
We'll go there right away.

495
00:25:57,500 --> 00:25:58,733
I'll bring backup.

496
00:25:58,733 --> 00:26:01,733
Search the entire area
and find Sam Jacinto.

497
00:26:01,733 --> 00:26:04,067
Find out what happened.

498
00:26:04,067 --> 00:26:05,267
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

499
00:26:05,267 --> 00:26:07,700
- Santos, come on.
- Let's move! Come on!

500
00:26:07,700 --> 00:26:08,767
Sir.

501
00:26:08,800 --> 00:26:14,533
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

502
00:26:16,233 --> 00:26:23,133
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

503
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:34,400
[BREATHES HEAVILY]

504
00:26:36,733 --> 00:26:43,733
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

505
00:26:43,767 --> 00:26:44,767
[BREATH QUIVERS]

506
00:26:45,767 --> 00:26:46,967
Auntie!

507
00:26:55,200 --> 00:26:56,533
Miss?

508
00:26:56,533 --> 00:26:57,900
Miss.

509
00:26:59,567 --> 00:27:00,633
[SAM WHIMPERS]

510
00:27:01,467 --> 00:27:02,500
Auntie!

511
00:27:05,667 --> 00:27:07,067
You're burning up.

512
00:27:07,067 --> 00:27:10,267
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

513
00:27:10,267 --> 00:27:11,367
[BLOWS AIR]

514
00:27:14,533 --> 00:27:21,500
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

515
00:27:22,133 --> 00:27:23,200
[HUFFS]

516
00:27:31,333 --> 00:27:32,300
- [BLOWS AIR]
- [SAM GRUNTS]

517
00:27:38,133 --> 00:27:39,467
She's cold.

518
00:27:46,100 --> 00:27:48,033
Miss? Miss?

519
00:27:51,100 --> 00:27:52,833
Her fever is really high!

520
00:27:55,333 --> 00:27:59,133
I'm sorry, miss,
but I have to do this.

521
00:27:59,133 --> 00:28:06,067
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

522
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:27,700
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

523
00:28:36,767 --> 00:28:39,133
<i>Victor Zafra
is our top priority.</i>

524
00:28:39,933 --> 00:28:42,333
<i>Whatever happens,
we need to take him</i>

525
00:28:42,333 --> 00:28:44,667
<i> to maximum security detention.</i>

526
00:28:44,667 --> 00:28:46,633
<i> Bring back my son.</i>

527
00:28:46,633 --> 00:28:48,667
<i>Team, hostile vehicles
approaching.</i>

528
00:28:48,667 --> 00:28:51,233
<i> - Stay alert.
- Guys, get ready to engage.</i>

529
00:28:51,233 --> 00:28:52,533
[GUNS COCK]

530
00:28:52,533 --> 00:28:53,667
<i> Stop them!</i>

531
00:28:53,667 --> 00:28:55,333
[GUNSHOTS]

532
00:28:55,333 --> 00:28:56,700
<i> Go! Secure Zafra!</i>

533
00:28:56,733 --> 00:28:58,100
[GUNSHOTS]

534
00:28:59,167 --> 00:29:02,633
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

535
00:29:04,233 --> 00:29:06,167
<i> Our men are armed and ready.</i>

536
00:29:06,167 --> 00:29:08,067
<i>I will make sure
Sam comes home.</i>

537
00:29:08,067 --> 00:29:09,567
<i>- Hand over Samantha.
- [GUNS COCK]</i>

538
00:29:09,567 --> 00:29:10,800
<i> And no one dies.</i>

539
00:29:10,800 --> 00:29:13,200
<i> You're in my turf, Ricardo.</i>

540
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:14,333
<i> Men!</i>

541
00:29:14,333 --> 00:29:17,733
<i>Do you still want to
make it out of here alive?</i>

542
00:29:17,733 --> 00:29:20,167
<i>When I entered the room,
something fell from above.</i>

543
00:29:20,167 --> 00:29:21,700
<i>That woman fell
through the roof.</i>

544
00:29:21,700 --> 00:29:23,533
<i> She's not
getting out of here alive.</i>

545
00:29:23,533 --> 00:29:24,700
<i> Keep your eyes peeled.</i>

546
00:29:24,700 --> 00:29:29,033
<i> Those men circling the area
are looking for her.</i>

547
00:29:29,067 --> 00:29:30,833
<i> I am willing to pay any amount</i>

548
00:29:30,833 --> 00:29:33,000
<i> to capture Samantha Jacinto.</i>

549
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:34,200
<i> She's in danger.</i>

550
00:29:34,200 --> 00:29:36,400
<i>We need to help her.
We need to protect her.</i>

551
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:39,200
<i> Who are you?! Who am I?!
Why am I here?!</i>

552
00:29:39,200 --> 00:29:41,533
<i> Love! It's me, Gabo!
Your husband!</i>
